    "body": "Review-fix round 3 pushed (head 8ca9fb6e, origin/main merged first; still a draft).\n\nBlocker fixed by the general fix: on a leaning move the excused kerf is now the cutter-radius disc about the unshifted tip, not about the band's shifted centre - in law (c), its hidden-stock backstop (`Rest::hidden_in_annulus` takes the band centre and the tip) and every (c3) sweep state. Upright the two coincide, so vertical verdicts are unchanged (pinned).\n\nThe review's reproduction now convicts: stepped body and plain slim r6 x 20 holder, tilted 30 deg into the wall at x 40, through (c) (`ShankHit{2, part:true}`) and through (c3) on a turning plunge whose end pose leans away (`SweepHit{2, part:true}`). The four tests fail on f74f878d's sim code and pass now. One existing assertion changed in kind only (`verify::a_swinging_head_sweeps_the_island_wall_mid_turn`: move 2 is now `ShankHit` from (c) instead of `SweepHit` from (c3) - its shank really stands in the island). No goldens moved. This also fixes #903 (`Fixes #903` added).\n",
