    "updated_at": "2026-11-11T22:33:40Z",
    "body": "Review-fix round 4 pushed (head e3d75b59, origin/main 3bd54fc9 merged first; still a draft).\n\nBlocker fixed: the `band_r <= r` skip in law (c) (reach.rs) and (c3) (sweep.rs) now applies only to an upright band. On a tilted move a plain or necked shank is judged, with the round-3 tip-centred kerf excusing the flutes' cut. The re-review's long-reach Ø8 mill (shank r4 8..38, 30 deg into the wall) and an r3.5 neck now convict through (c) (`ShankHit{2, part:true}`) and through (c3) on a turning plunge whose end pose leans away (`SweepHit{2, part:true}`); both pins fail on 8ca9fb6e's sim code. Upright verdicts with the same tools are pinned unchanged.\n\nOver-report check: sim `--tests`, the app multiaxis/rotary/posed/golden suites and motion swarf/pivot5d/flow/multiaxis/rotary suites all pass with no existing assertion, golden or snapshot changed (list in the PR body).\n",
